        "id": 129733,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-29T14:08:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If you find an infinite loop, chances are you are playing it wrong. It's a standard rule of thumb.</p><p>Ronway is correct. All those one-shots stay in play until they completely resolve. Newest actions always resolve first, so the new cards that get played start being resolved before the old ones finish. Playing Akash is a great way to practice this, as she consistantly has a lot of one-shots with multiple parts that string in the play area like this.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:04:43.680Z",
